Now remove RED_PLACES (unused) to avoid confusion? It's fine but lint no matter. Leave.

Now update setCaseChrome/renderCase for scene render & hotspots. Current setCaseChrome last line `$('#sceneArt').dataset.place = c.location.place;` must be removed (location.place undefined). Replace with nothing. We'll render in renderCase.

`renderCase()`:
```
setCaseChrome();
$('#sceneCanvas').innerHTML = renderScene(c.location);
$$('.hotspot').forEach(btn => {
  const key=...
  const meta=stationOf(c.location,key);
  const pt=getStationPoint(c.location,key);
  btn.style.left=pt.x+'%'; btn.style.top=pt.y+'%';
  btn.dataset.side = pt.y > 56 ? 'top' : 'bottom';
  btn.querySelector('.tag').textContent = meta.label;
});
```
But renderCase doesn't declare c; setCaseChrome gets state.caseData. Add `const c = state.caseData;` at start.

`renderSceneState` use meta.label and meta.name.

`renderZoom` use meta:
```
const meta=stationOf(c.location,key);
...
`EXHIBIT ${obj.exhibit} · ${meta.label}`
...
$('#zoomObject').textContent = meta.label;
...
aria-label `Close-up of ${meta.name}`
```

`renderBoard` label meta in two places.

Also hotspot aria label at initial HTML static; renderCase should set it via renderSceneState perhaps. `renderCase` calls `renderBoard` and sets tags; call `renderSceneState()` at end? It currently duplicates logic. Could simply set tags and labels then renderBoard. renderSceneState also updates clueProgress. We can call `renderSceneState()` after setting positions (state.found empty at startCase). But renderCase is called before state.found? startCase sets found then renderCase. Good. Use `renderCase` to set positions + then renderSceneState(); remove manual tag loop. But found set may not be empty if renderCase called later? Only startCase. Fine.

Let's implement.

Also `renderScene` should be called each new case. InnerHTML parsing of SVG in a div works (HTML parser handles svg). Yes.

Now `setCaseChrome` also sets `#sceneArt.dataset.place`; remove. We can set `dataset.scene = c.location.scene` if useful.

Let's edit.

