Office fine.

Now capture all 24 scenes. Need to force location per scene. Use page.evaluate with index:
```
const all = LOCATIONS.slice();
previousLocation = null;
LOCATIONS.length=0; LOCATIONS.push(all[i]);
state.caseData = makeCase();
LOCATIONS.length=0; LOCATIONS.push(...all);
state.found=new Set(); state.currentObject=null;
renderCase(); showScreen('scene');
```
But makeCase's previousLocation: set null first. Good. Note `previousLocation` declared `let` at top-level; assigning from evaluate works? Top-level let is in global lexical environment; page.evaluate function executes in global scope, can assign `previousLocation = null`? It resolves the binding, yes. Let's test.

Then screenshot `#sceneArt` element (400-ish px). Also take full-screen for a few.

Create script for all scenes at 390x844. Save to /tmp/opencode/shots/scenes/XX-scene.png. Also collect per-scene overflow and overlaps? We can compute bounding boxes of hotspot tags and check intersections. That's valuable. Compute `getBoundingClientRect` of `.hotspot .tag` and art rect; check tag collisions with each other. Also check if tag extends outside scene-art. We'll log warnings.

Let's write.

