4.7557 = 358/77.727 / (x/400) → x/400=0.9684 → x=387.4. So stage.width must have been 387.4. The scene art width of 400.93 was from the earlier `zoomrect` at 390x844 when on the zoom screen? Wait `zoomrect` measured sceneArt while on the scene screen after goScene, giving 400.93. But at renderZoom time, the scene screen is inactive, its layout may still be constrained by the screen's padding? Hmm, if inactive screens are `visibility:hidden` with `display:flex`? The 387.4 could be the scene art width when the scene screen is inactive due to a scrollbar? Or `.scene-art` width formula uses cqh which depends on container query height of the device; the screen may be larger/smaller when inactive? Another possibility: renderZoom is called before `beginZoomIn`, while `.screen-zoom` is active; the scene screen is inactive but still has `width:min(112%,470px,calc((100cqh - 178px) * .8))`. cqh is relative to `.device` container, constant across screens. So 400.93 should be the same. Why 387.4?

