content.text:
Now update `cancelZoomTransit` to roll back the pre-activated scene if canceling before finish. Currently:

```js
function cancelZoomTransit() {
  if (!zoomTransit) return;
  const { timer, cleanup } = zoomTransit;
  if (timer) clearTimeout(timer);
  if (cleanup) clearTimeout(cleanup);
  zoomTransit = null;
  ...
  $('#screen-zoom').classList.remove('is-transit');
}
```

Add mode capture and rollback. But watch: when `cancelZoomTransit` is called by `showScreen('board')` during a zoom-out animation, state.screen is 'zoom' (because finish not yet called). Rollback scene. When called by `showScreen('office')` etc. Fine. When called after finish but before cleanup (e.g., state.screen==='scene', zoomTransit still exists), don't rollback.

Also, during a zoom-in cancel (mode 'in'), the scene screen wasn't pre-activated; no rollback.

Implementation:
```js
const mode = zoomTransit.mode;
...
if (mode === 'out' && state.screen === 'zoom') {
  $('#screen-scene').classList.remove('is-active','is-instant');
}
```
But careful ordering: `showScreen('board')` calls cancel *before* it sets state.screen='board'. So state.screen is 'zoom' → rollback. Good.

At cleanup after finish, state.screen is 'scene' → no rollback; also we should remove is-instant there (already done).

Also reset frame opacity/veil (already). And `transit` opacity? We never set transit inline. Fine.

Let's edit.

