content.text:
Now cleanup and cancel need to cancel the zoomScreen animations. In beginZoomOut cleanup:
```js
zoomScreen.classList.remove('is-leaving');
```
Add before: `zoomScreen.getAnimations().forEach((a) => a.cancel());`.
In cancel: same when mode out? The zoom screen fade animation only exists for mode out. Add unconditionally? If mode in, the zoom screen might have a normal fade animation from `showScreen` transition—those are CSS transitions and `getAnimations()` includes them. Canceling could make the screen jump visible. Only do it for mode out. In cancel's rollback block:
```js
if (mode === 'out' && state.screen === 'zoom') {
  $('#screen-zoom').getAnimations().forEach((a)=>a.cancel());
  $('#screen-zoom').classList.remove('is-leaving');
  ...
}
```
Also in openObject defensive removal: if leftover, cancel. Add:
```js
const zoomEl = $('#screen-zoom');
zoomEl.getAnimations().forEach((a)=>a.cancel());
zoomEl.classList.remove('is-leaving');
```
But openObject is called when a new zoom starts; there shouldn't be leftover if cleanup ran. Defensive cancel might cancel the scene/zoom screen's CSS transitions from showScreen, but we're about to set is-transit and show zoom; okay. Better only cancel if `is-leaving` present:
```js
