content.text:
Now CSS. Add styles after `.zoom-canvas svg` perhaps.

Let's design exact CSS:

```
.zoom-spots{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:5;pointer-events:none}
.search-spot{
  position:absolute;width:46px;height:46px;margin:-23px 0 0 -23px;border-radius:50%;
  pointer-events:auto;background:none;border:0;padding:0;color:inherit;
}
.search-spot .glint{
  position:absolute;left:50%;top:50%;width:11px;height:11px;margin:-5.5px;
  transform:rotate(45deg);
  background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(247,223,168,.9),rgba(190,145,72,.35));
  border:1px solid rgba(248,226,178,.95);
  box-shadow:0 0 12px rgba(232,196,124,.8),0 0 28px rgba(201,161,94,.35);
}
.search-spot .glint::before{
  content:"";position:absolute;inset:-9px;border:1px solid rgba(226,194,134,.35);border-radius:50%;
  transform:rotate(-45deg);
  animation:spotPulse 2.8s ease-out infinite;
}
@keyframes spotPulse{
  0%,100%{transform:rotate(-45deg) scale(1);opacity:.8}
  50%{transform:rotate(-45deg) scale(1.35);opacity:.28}
}
.search-spot .spot-tag{
  position:absolute;left:50%;top:calc(100% - 2px);transform:translateX(-50%);
  padding:2.5px 5px;background:rgba(8,6,5,.86);border:1px solid rgba(201,161,94,.34);
  color:var(--gold);font-size:6.4px;letter-spacing:.14em;line-height:1;white-space:nowrap;
  text-transform:uppercase;text-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.8);pointer-events:none;
}
.search-spot[data-side="top"] .spot-tag{top:auto;bottom:calc(100% - 2px)}
.search-spot[data-side="left"] .spot-tag{left:auto;right:calc(50% + 7px);top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%)}
.search-spot[data-side="right"] .spot-tag{left:calc(50% + 7px);right:auto;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%)}
.scene... no
.search-spot[data-searched="true"] .glint{opacity:.32;box-shadow:none;border-style:dashed;background:rgba(226,194,134,.18)}
.search-spot[data-searched="true"] .glint::before{animation:none;opacity:.2}
.search-spot[data-searched="true"] .spot-tag{opacity:.55}
.search-spot.is-clue .glint{opacity:1;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f6d998,#b07a2f);box-shadow:0 0 16px rgba(246,217,152,.95),0 0 36px rgba(201,161,94,.5)}
.search-spot.is-clue .spot-tag{color:#f6e6c2;border-color:rgba(243,222,180,.65);background:rgba(30,18,8,.92)}
.zoom-spots.is-laying-out .spot-tag{transition:none}
.search-spot:focus-visible{outline:2px solid rgba(243,222,180,.9);outline-offset:2px}
```

`:focus-visible` on the round button may create a circle outline around the 46px target, good.

Press effect:
```
.search-spot:active .glint{transform:rotate(45deg) scale(.78)}
```

Clue sheet searching style:
```
.clue-sheet.is-searching .clue-text{color:#3c2f1e;font-style:italic}
.clue-sheet.is-searching .gun-tag{display:none}
```
Actually `.gun-tag` display toggles only with `.is-gun`; `.is-searching` not needed. But remove is-gun. Fine.

`#zoomStatus.ok{color:#3c5b2e;font-weight:600}`. Base `.logged{color:#5b452c}`.

Fade out in leaving rule: add `.zoom-spots` to the selector list.

On very small heights maybe tags 6px. Existing media max-height 670 adjusts zoom? Let's view around 991.

