const token = $('.clue-find', layer);
...
const pos = spotPixel(plan, plan.clueSpot, frame, layerBox, bayBox)
const x=clamp(pos.x, 33, layerBox.width-33)
const y=clamp(pos.y, 31, layerBox.height-31)
token.style.left...
token.style.top...
token.dataset.tag = y > layerBox.height - 46 ? 'top' : 'bottom';
```
The token card bottom at y+27; tag below at y+28..y+40. If layer height 300, y clamped 269; tag bottom 309 > 300. So set data-tag top when y > height - 44. With y=269, tag top? tag at bottom of button (100%+1 = y+28) → overflow; set top when y > height - 44. Good.
But x clamp 33; token width 54, so left 33-27=6; tag width maybe 30, centered at 33 -> 18..48, inside. Good.
- At top y=31, token top=4; tag below at 59, inside. Good.

